<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanacpachap cussicuinin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">composed between <a href="/years/1620">1620</a> and <a href="/years/1631">1631</a>; published <a href="/years/1631">1631</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Hanacpachap cussicuinin (modern orthography: Hanaq pachap kusikuynin)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Hanacpachap cussicuinin&quot; is a processional hymn to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quechua">Quechua</a> language of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, written in a largely European style of sacred music. It was composed between 1620 and 1631 by Juan Pérez de Bocanegra, a Franciscan priest who was also chief examiner of native languages for the Archdiocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cuzco</a>, and published in 1631 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>.</p></div>
